/*!

\mainpage The Draco Documentation System
\version Draco-@Draco_VERSION_FULL@

\par Executive Summary

Draco is a C++ radiation transport component library developed by CAI-2, [Los Alamos National
Laboratory](https://www.lanl.gov). In addition to providing infrastructure for radiation transport
code development, Draco serves as a "model Development Environment (DE)" for code development
activities within CAI-2.  Most CAI-2 code projects are based on the coding standards, idioms, style,
organization, and architecture of Draco.

\par Authors:

@AUTHOR_LIST@

\par Resources

To get started building Draco see \ref build_system  or [build
system](https://re-git.lanl.gov/draco/draco/-/wikis/Common_Configure_Options).
Package overviews can be found in the <a href="pages.html">Related Pages</a>
section of the documentation. Also see:

- <a href=https://github.com/lanl/Draco>Draco on GitHub</a>.
- <a href=http://re-git.lanl.gov/draco/draco>Draco project management</a>.
- <a href=https://re-cdash.lanl.gov/index.php?project=Draco>Draco regression reporting on CDash</a>.
- Draco mailing list, draco@lanl.gov

\par Versions and Platforms

\msc

   # The entities
   ML, SN, TT, Sierra, ElCap, xrds, CTS2, Venado, ATS5;

   # Small gap before the boxes
   |||;

   # Next items on same line due to ','
